  "body": "A plugin's prepaid wallet window (#3950: `{name: \"积分\", balance: 6291, unit: \"积分\"}`, no `used`, no `aside`) is kept in quota history as a flat 100%-left line.\n\n`quotaOfPlugin` (internal/provider/plugin_usage.go) keeps the balance and, on purpose, makes the window neither `Text` nor `Aside`, so routing reads it (#3950). Its `Used` stays 0. `pointOf` (internal/provider/quota_history.go) draws any window that isn't Text, Unlimited or a Family, has a name and a Used that isn't NaN, so every reading of a SuperMagic account adds a point of `Left: 100` for its balance window, and the quota history chart draws a line that says nothing is ever used.\n\nThis is the non-aside sibling of #4825 (an aside window with no `used`), which is fixed by a `noShare` flag that `pointOf` refuses. The #4825 fix leaves the wallet as it is because `noShare` is set on aside windows only. Possible fix: also set `noShare` on a window with a `balance` and no `used`, or have `pointOf` refuse `w.Balance != nil` when no share was told. If a wallet should have a history at all, that would be a balance-over-time line (balance-history.json?), not a percent left.\n\nFound in ggbdpq's review of #4825, from reading the code; not reproduced with a real SuperMagic account. A test: `quotaOfPlugin` over `{\"windows\":[{\"name\":\"积分\",\"balance\":6291,\"unit\":\"积分\"}]}`, then `pointOf` on its window, should give no point.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
