     "body": "49c99e18d (#4612, ggbdpq) makes quota history draw a window set aside for routing, and marks Factory's \"Extra usage\" `Text` so it isn't drawn as a line.\n\n`pointOf` (internal/provider/quota_history.go) still draws any window that isn't Text, Unlimited or a Family, has a name, and has a Used that isn't NaN. A plugin's aside row that has only a display or an amount, and no used share, comes in with Used 0, so it is drawn as a flat 100% left line. Factory was fixed at its source. Every other plugin that reports such a row has the same problem.\n\nPossible fixes: skip a window with no Used reading (that needs a way to tell \"0 used\" from \"not said\"), or have the plugin usage reader mark such rows Text. Found in the review of #4612. Not reproduced with a real plugin.\n",
