   "body": "Fixed on branch [fix/4831-wallet-balance-no-line](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/4831-wallet-balance-no-line) (head `6a7938676`, on main `8abdf53a8`). This is the non-aside sibling of #4825 (aside windows, landed in ca1fc43fc / v0.1.2664, which this fix leaves as it is).\n\n**Root cause**: `quotaOfPlugin` keeps a wallet window on purpose as a window routing reads (#3950) — `{name:\"积分\", balance:6291, unit:\"积分\"}`, no `used`, not `aside` — so its `Used` stays 0 with no flag set. `pointOf` draws any window that isn't Text, Unlimited or a Family, has a name and a Used that isn't NaN, so every reading added a point of `Left: 100` for the balance window and the chart drew the flat line. #4825's `noShare` covered aside windows only (`else if x.Aside`), because routing keys on `Aside` alone; the wallet fell through the `else if x.Balance == nil` branch with neither.\n\n**Fix**: the issue's first suggested option — `quotaOfPlugin` sets `noShare` on a window whose used the plugin left out when it is set aside *or* tells a balance. Its Used is 0 for want of a share said, not a reading at 0; `pointOf` already refuses `noShare`. A wallet that said a share keeps its line; routing still knows the wallet by its balance (`Allowance.Left`, asserted); the card still shows the figure (`BalanceText`). The field comment, `pointOf`'s comment and docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md say so beside the aside rule. `plugin_usage.go` is the only producer of `QuotaWindow.Balance`, so no sibling reader needed the same change. A balance-over-time line stays open, as the issue frames it — that would be balance-history.json's story, not a percent left.\n\n**Verification** (linux/amd64, go1.27.3, `nogui`): the issue's own test shape — new `TestWalletWindowWithoutUsedDrawsNoLine` runs `quotaOfPlugin` over `{\"windows\":[{\"name\":\"积分\",\"balance\":6291,\"unit\":\"积分\"}, …]}` and `pointOf` on its window — is red on clean main (a point and a history line for 积分) and ok after, end to end through `noteQuotaHistory` and `QuotaHistories` (only the share-said wallet's line remains) with `Allowance.Left` unchanged; red again with `plugin_usage.go` back at main's. `go test ./internal/provider -tags nogui -count=1` ok; gofmt clean; linux and windows vet clean; builds ok.\n\n**Not tried**: a real SuperMagic account; the chart in a browser — the change stops the fictitious points from reaching quota-history.json, and the chart draws what the API returns.\n\nGenerated-by: GLM-5.3 (ZCode)\n",
